# Git LFS. Screen recordings are binary and get re-recorded, so every take git
# stores is a whole extra copy that can never be removed without rewriting
# history. Pointers keep the history light; the bytes live in LFS and are
# fetched only for the revision being checked out.
#
# The six recordings already in history at 738d133 stay as ordinary blobs -
# that weight is spent. Everything from here on is a pointer.
# LFS hooks live in .husky/, not .git/hooks, because this repository sets
# core.hooksPath. See .husky/pre-push.
*.mp4 filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
apps/web/public/guide/*.png filter=lfs diff=lfs merge=lfs -text
